+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias.  An optional description body may be used to
+   document the alias.  Type aliases may be documented at module level or
+   inside a class; the directive does not contain nested object declarations.
+
+   The optional ``canonical`` option describes the type represented by the
+   alias.  When provided, it appears after the alias name in the signature and
+   is parsed as a type annotation, so referenced types can be cross-referenced.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      The type represented by the alias.  This optional expression appears in
+      the directive signature.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined.  The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
